-- Quest map areas: link old-format areas to their objective so the client hides them once the objective is done
-- In 5.4.8 SMSG_QUEST_POI_QUERY_RESPONSE carries each area's objective index and quest objective id, and the client hides
-- an area whose objective is complete. 9292 of mop's areas have them (index = quest_objective.index, id = quest_objective.id,
-- as the retail TDB 1210). 7571 still had the Cataclysm numbering (0-3 creature/object slots, 4-9 item slots) and objective
-- id 0, so they never cleared (found on Stones of Binding 26041: a looted key's area stayed on the map).
-- Each old-format area is mapped to the k-th creature/object or item objective of its quest; only the 5352 areas whose
-- mapped (index, id) is exactly a pair the retail TDB 1210 has for that quest are changed. The other 2219 (no matching
-- objective, no TDB row, or a different pair in the TDB) are left as they were. Turn-in areas (-1) are not touched.
